  "semantic_contract": "Shared app WORD bounds E4/E6/E8/EA are initialized to16/303/30/128 at3410 and consumed by clear/horizon bands, model and HUD clipping, line clipping6096/609A and the20-point field renderer4E04A. Bounds comparisons include their endpoints; this names the original contract, not arbitrary-input safety. Active model scale WORD1AA receives object BYTE1D low4bits at4A2A/5338, viewer digits0..8, defaults4/7 and an overlay increment; vertex arithmetic shifts and projected-radius scaling consume it. BYTE1F2 samples alternate hardware8260 bit1 then becomes0/FF while selecting mode0/mode1 helpers and asset conversion; no alternate-platform run is claimed. Point-field plane stride WORD1A2 is2000 for Amiga,2 for alternate mode0 and0 for mode1, used for successive plane WORD accesses.4DFC8 loops20 times writing XYZ WORD triplets at appBC6 and clears20 previous-view triplets at appC3E.4E04A reads20 world triplets, subtracts player position, rotates, caches view XYZ atC3E and uses old triples for fast-flight trails; rejection recycles the current point. These are finite original producer/consumer extents, not universal object/model identities or a claim of absent aliases. App base follows the existing A6/layout contract; fallback references remain labelled assumptions, not independent all-path address proofs. Raw displacements and original timing/control flow are unchanged.",
